      "content": "My assessment of the \"slight logical gap\" is based on the strict standards of advanced theoretical physics, where every step of a proof must be explicitly justified, not just strongly implied. To argue that it is *not* a deal-breaker would be misleading, as a critical review could indeed exploit that unstated assumption to challenge the conclusion.\n\nHowever, if the primary goal is to meet a fixed marketing deadline and avoid immediate high-stakes conflict, the next best action is to frame this not as a \"fatal flaw,\" but as a \"necessary clarification for complete technical precision.\" You could justify a highly focused, targeted \"minor revision request\" to the authors to *clarify* that limit rather than demanding a total re-proof to maintain the appearance of forward momentum.",
